@* AdminUsers.razor — Phase 6.1

   Staff-facing user-management page at route `/Admin/Users`. Reached from
   the sidebar's "Admin → Manage Users" link (already wired in
   MainLayout.razor, role-gated to Admin/Manager). The page is also
   independently gated by [Authorize(Roles=...)] as defense-in-depth.

   PURPOSE:
     This page is the admin/manager's view of every user in the system
     (staff and customers). It exists so they can:
       1. See ALL users in a compact, paginated table (not a single
          customer-by-customer drill-down).
       2. Search by Worker ID or Full Name (server-side filter).
       3. Filter by active/inactive status.
       4. Activate or Deactivate a user (soft-delete / restore).
       5. Reset a user's password (Admin only — managers cannot reset
          passwords, per ResetUserPasswordCommand's [RequireRoles(Admin)]).

   WHAT THIS PAGE DOES NOT DO (out of scope for v1 — see Phase 6.2+):
     - Create user UI (form for CreateStaffCommand / CreateCustomerCommand).
       The commands + handlers already exist; the create-user FORM is
       deferred. For now, users are seeded via the DB seed or created via
       direct API calls.
     - User detail page with role assignment UI (AssignUserRoleCommand /
       RemoveUserRoleCommand exist; the UI is deferred). For now, role
       changes require DB access.
     - Edit user full name (UpdateUserFullNameCommand exists; UI deferred).
     - Group management (AssignUserToGroupCommand / RemoveUserFromGroupCommand
       exist; UI deferred).
     - Group-name dropdown filter (would need a "list all groups" query,
       which doesn't exist yet — currently GetCustomersByGroupQuery goes
       the other direction).

   LAYOUT:
     1. Page header: title + (deferred) "Create user" button placeholder.
     2. Filter bar: search box + activity-status dropdown.
     3. Loading / error / empty / table states.
     4. User table: RadzenDataGrid (no built-in pager) with columns for
        Worker ID, Full Name, Gender, Group (manager+admin only — never
        shown to employees, but employees can't reach this page anyway),
        Status (active/inactive badge), and an actions column.
     5. Manual pager (Prev / page numbers / Next + total count).

   ROLE-RESOLUTION PATTERN (CRITICAL):
     _isAdmin is computed via AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync()
     in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via ICurrentUserService.IsInRole. The
     ICurrentUserService reads from IHttpContextAccessor.HttpContext,
     which is NULL over the SignalR circuit in interactive Blazor Server
     mode (HttpContext only exists during the initial prerender request).
     AuthStateProvider reads from the Blazor circuit's persistent auth
     state, which IS preserved across circuit interactions.

     The same pattern is used in Sales.razor (Phase 4.2) and
     SaleDetail.razor (Phase 4.3) — see those files for the longer
     explanation. The Wolverine command handlers ALSO enforce
     [RequireRoles] server-side as defense-in-depth, so even if the
     client-side role check is wrong, the server still rejects the call.

   DATA LOADING:
     OnInitializedAsync: resolve the current user's Id + Admin role, then
     load the first page of users via GetUsersPaginatedQuery. Filter
     changes reset the page to 1 and re-query.

   ACTIVATE / DEACTIVATE FLOW:
     - A single toggle button per row. When the user is Active, the button
       shows "Deactivate" (Danger outlined, block icon). When Inactive, it
       shows "Activate" (Success outlined, check icon).
     - Self-deactivation is blocked client-side (the button is hidden on
       the current user's own row) AND server-side (the handler rejects it
       with a friendly message). The client-side check is purely UX —
       without it, the user would click, see an error toast, and have to
       re-think; with it, the button just isn't there.
     - On click: confirm via JS confirm() (a destructive action deserves
       one click of friction), then dispatch the appropriate command,
       toast on success, reload the grid.

   RESET PASSWORD FLOW:
     - Admin-only (button hidden from Managers). The button is also hidden
       on the current user's own row — admins can technically reset their
       own password via this command (the handler doesn't block it), but
       it's a confusing UX so we don't offer it. Admins should use the
       self-service password change flow (deferred) instead.
     - On click: prompt via JS prompt() for the new password (same pattern
       as AdminProducts.razor's restock flow). The handler defers password
       complexity validation to ASP.NET Identity's configured rules —
       client-side we just check it's non-empty and at least 8 chars to
       catch obvious typos before the round-trip.
     - On success: toast. On failure: toast with the handler's error
       message (Identity's error descriptions are user-friendly enough).

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings go through IStringLocalizer<AdminUsers>
     (Loc). Keys are defined in AdminUsers.en-US.resx +
     AdminUsers.fa-IR.resx. RTL is handled at the html dir level by
     MainLayout based on the current culture.

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed — no EditForm. All actions use Wolverine command dispatch
     over the Blazor circuit. The circuit's anti-forgery token covers
     this case. *@

@page "/Admin/Users"
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = "Admin,Manager")]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Users.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ActivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.DeactivateUser
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Commands.ResetUserPassword
@using TakOne.Application.Users.Queries.GetUsersPaginated
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.WebUI.Services
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<AdminUsers> Loc
@inject AuthenticationStateProvider AuthStateProvider
@inject ToastService Toast
@inject IJSRuntime JS

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            .admin-header {
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: space-between;
                gap: 1rem;
                flex-wrap: wrap;
            }

            .worker-id-cell {
                font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 0.875rem;
            }

            .user-name-cell {
                font-weight: 500;
            }

            .group-cell-none {
                color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                font-style: italic;
            }

            .row-actions {
                display: flex;
                gap: 0.25rem;
                justify-content: flex-end;
                align-items: center;
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ── *@
    <div class="admin-header">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="group" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["CreateUserButton"]"
                      Icon="person_add"
                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                      Variant="Variant.Filled"
                      Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Users/Create", forceLoad: false))" />
    </div>

    @* ── Filter bar ── *@
    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1rem;">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                     AlignItems="AlignItems.End"
                     JustifyContent="JustifyContent.SpaceBetween"
                     Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                     Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["SearchLabel"]" Style="flex: 1 1 240px; min-width: 200px;">
                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_searchTerm"
                               @bind-Value:after="OnSearchChanged"
                               Placeholder="@Loc["SearchPlaceholder"]"
                               TValue="string" />
            </RadzenFormField>

            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["StatusLabel"]" Style="flex: 0 1 200px; min-width: 160px;">
                <RadzenDropDown Value="_activityFilter"
                                Data="_activityFilterOptions"
                                TValue="ActivityFilter"
                                TextProperty="Label"
                                ValueProperty="Value"
                                ValueChanged="@OnActivityFilterChanged"
                                Style="width: 100%;" />
            </RadzenFormField>
        </RadzenStack>
    </RadzenCard>

    @* ── Loading spinner ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingText"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error banner ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadUsersAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Empty state (no users at all) ── *@
    else if (_users.Count == 0 && !HasActiveFilters())
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 3rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="person_off" Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyMessage"]"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 420px;" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Empty state (filters yielded nothing) ── *@
    else if (_users.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 3rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="search_off" Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyFilteredTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyFilteredMessage"]"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 420px;" />
                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ClearFiltersButton"]"
                              Icon="filter_alt_off"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Base"
                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                              Click="@ClearFiltersAsync" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── User table ── *@
    else
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 0.5rem;">
            <RadzenDataGrid Data="@_users"
                            AllowSorting="false"
                            AllowPaging="false"
                            Style="width: 100%;"
                            RowRender="@OnRowRender">
                <Columns>
                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="WorkerId"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColWorkerId"]"
                                          Width="160px">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <span class="worker-id-cell">@user.WorkerId</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="FullName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColFullName"]"
                                          Width="*">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <span class="user-name-cell">@user.FullName</span>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="Gender"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColGender"]"
                                          Width="120px">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            @GetGenderLabel(user.Gender)
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="GroupName"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColGroup"]"
                                          Width="180px">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            @if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(user.GroupName))
                            {
                                <span class="group-cell-none">@Loc["GroupNone"]</span>
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@user.GroupName"
                                             BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Base"
                                             IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Property="IsActive"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColStatus"]"
                                          Width="120px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            @if (user.IsActive)
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusActiveBadge"]"
                                             BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Success"
                                             IsPill="true" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenBadge Text="@Loc["StatusInactiveBadge"]"
                                             BadgeStyle="BadgeStyle.Light"
                                             IsPill="true" />
                            }
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>

                    <RadzenDataGridColumn TItem="UserListItemDto"
                                          Title="@Loc["ColActions"]"
                                          Width="180px"
                                          TextAlign="TextAlign.Center"
                                          Sortable="false">
                        <Template Context="user">
                            <div class="row-actions">
                                @* Activate / Deactivate toggle.
                                   Hidden on the current user's own row —
                                   self-deactivation is rejected by the
                                   handler anyway, but the button adds
                                   confusing UX so we just don't show it. *@
                                @if (user.Id != _currentUserId)
                                {
                                    @if (user.IsActive)
                                    {
                                        <RadzenButton Icon="block"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Danger"
                                                      title="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                      aria-label="@Loc["ActionDeactivate"]"
                                                      Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                      Click="@(() => HandleDeactivateAsync(user))" />
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        <RadzenButton Icon="check_circle"
                                                      Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Success"
                                                      title="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                                      aria-label="@Loc["ActionActivate"]"
                                                      Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                      Click="@(() => HandleActivateAsync(user))" />
                                    }
                                }

                                @* Reset password — Admin only.
                                   Hidden from Managers (button not rendered)
                                   AND hidden on the current user's own row
                                   (admin self-reset is technically allowed
                                   by the handler but confusing UX). The
                                   server-side [RequireRoles(Admin)] is the
                                   real guard; this is UX-only. *@
                                @if (_isAdmin && user.Id != _currentUserId)
                                {
                                    <RadzenButton Icon="vpn_key"
                                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                                  ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Warning"
                                                  title="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                                  aria-label="@Loc["ActionResetPassword"]"
                                                  Disabled="@(_isBusyUserId == user.Id)"
                                                  Click="@(() => HandleResetPasswordAsync(user))" />
                                }
                            </div>
                        </Template>
                    </RadzenDataGridColumn>
                </Columns>
            </RadzenDataGrid>

            @* ── Pager ──
               Manual pager (Prev / page numbers / Next) — same approach as
               the /Sales list page. Operates on PaginatedResult metadata
               from the backend (true server-side paging). *@
            @if (_totalCount > _pageSize)
            {
                <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                             JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                             AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                             Gap="0.5rem"
                             Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                             Style="margin-top: 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                    <RadzenButton Icon="chevron_left"
                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                  Disabled="@(_pageNumber <= 1)"
                                  Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(_pageNumber - 1))" />

                    @{
                        var totalPages = (int)Math.Ceiling((double)_totalCount / _pageSize);
                        var startPage = Math.Max(1, _pageNumber - 2);
                        var endPage = Math.Min(totalPages, startPage + 4);
                        if (endPage - startPage < 4) startPage = Math.Max(1, endPage - 4);
                    }

                    @for (var p = startPage; p <= endPage; p++)
                    {
                        var page = p;
                        <RadzenButton Text="@(page.ToString())"
                                      Variant="@(page == _pageNumber ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Text)"
                                      ButtonStyle="@(page == _pageNumber ? ButtonStyle.Primary : ButtonStyle.Base)"
                                      Disabled="@(_isLoading)"
                                      Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(page))" />
                    }

                    <RadzenButton Icon="chevron_right"
                                  Variant="Variant.Text"
                                  Disabled="@(_pageNumber >= Math.Ceiling((double)_totalCount / _pageSize))"
                                  Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(_pageNumber + 1))" />

                    <RadzenText Text="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["PageInfoFormat"], _pageNumber, totalPages, _totalCount)"
                                TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                                Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-left: 0.5rem;" />
                </RadzenStack>
            }
        </RadzenCard>
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private List<UserListItemDto> _users = new();

    private string _searchTerm = string.Empty;
    private ActivityFilter _activityFilter = ActivityFilter.All;

    private const int _pageSize = 20;
    private int _pageNumber = 1;
    private int _totalCount;

    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The Id of the user whose action button is currently in flight.
    /// Null when no action is pending. Used to disable that row's action
    /// buttons while the round-trip is in progress (prevents double-clicks).
    /// </summary>
    private Guid? _isBusyUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// The current user's Id — used to hide self-action buttons
    /// (self-deactivation, self-password-reset) on the user's own row.
    /// Resolved once in OnInitializedAsync.
    /// </summary>
    private Guid _currentUserId;

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the current user is in the Admin role. Computed via
    /// AuthenticationStateProvider in OnInitializedAsync — NOT via
    /// ICurrentUserService.IsInRole (which returns false for everyone in
    /// interactive Blazor Server mode because HttpContext is null over
    /// the SignalR circuit). See the file-header comment for the full
    /// explanation.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isAdmin;

    private List<ActivityFilterOption> _activityFilterOptions = new();

    private sealed class ActivityFilterOption
    {
        public ActivityFilter Value { get; init; }
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    private enum ActivityFilter
    {
        All,
        Active,
        Inactive
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Populate the activity-filter dropdown options from localizer.
        _activityFilterOptions = new List<ActivityFilterOption>
        {
            new() { Value = ActivityFilter.All,      Label = Loc["StatusAll"] },
            new() { Value = ActivityFilter.Active,   Label = Loc["StatusActive"] },
            new() { Value = ActivityFilter.Inactive, Label = Loc["StatusInactive"] }
        };

        // Resolve the current user's Id + Admin role via the Blazor auth
        // state (NOT ICurrentUserService — see file-header comment).
        try
        {
            var authState = await AuthStateProvider.GetAuthenticationStateAsync();
            var user = authState.User;

            if (user?.Identity?.IsAuthenticated == true)
            {
                // The UserId claim is set by our custom IClaimsPrincipalFactory
                // in the Infrastructure layer — it's the Domain User's Guid Id.
                var idClaim = user.FindFirst("UserId")?.Value
                              ?? user.FindFirst(System.Security.Claims.ClaimTypes.NameIdentifier)?.Value;
                if (Guid.TryParse(idClaim, out var parsedId))
                {
                    _currentUserId = parsedId;
                }

                _isAdmin = user.IsInRole(Roles.Admin);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            // Non-fatal — _currentUserId stays Guid.Empty (no self-action
            // buttons hidden, which is safe but slightly worse UX) and
            // _isAdmin stays false (Reset Password button hidden — safer
            // fallback if role resolution fails).
        }

        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadUsersAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var query = new GetUsersPaginatedQuery
            {
                PageNumber = _pageNumber,
                PageSize = _pageSize,
                SearchTerm = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_searchTerm) ? null : _searchTerm.Trim(),
                IsActive = _activityFilter switch
                {
                    ActivityFilter.Active => true,
                    ActivityFilter.Inactive => false,
                    _ => null
                }
            };

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<PaginatedResult<UserListItemDto>>(query);

            _users = result.Items.ToList();
            _totalCount = result.TotalCount;

            // If we paginated past the last page (e.g. after a deactivation
            // reduced the total count), reset to page 1 and retry once.
            if (_users.Count == 0 && _pageNumber > 1)
            {
                _pageNumber = 1;
                await LoadUsersAsync();
                return;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_FailedToLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Filter handlers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task OnSearchChanged()
    {
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    private async Task OnActivityFilterChanged(ActivityFilter filter)
    {
        _activityFilter = filter;
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    private async Task OnPageChanged(int newPage)
    {
        _pageNumber = newPage;
        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    private async Task ClearFiltersAsync()
    {
        _searchTerm = string.Empty;
        _activityFilter = ActivityFilter.All;
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadUsersAsync();
    }

    private bool HasActiveFilters()
        => !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_searchTerm) || _activityFilter != ActivityFilter.All;

    // ── Activate / Deactivate ───────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task HandleDeactivateAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        // JS confirm() — destructive action deserves one click of friction.
        // The handler also rejects self-deactivation as defense-in-depth,
        // but we hide the button on the user's own row anyway (see markup).
        var confirmMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ConfirmDeactivate"],
            user.FullName,
            user.WorkerId);

        var confirmed = await JS.InvokeAsync<bool>("confirm", confirmMessage);
        if (!confirmed) return;

        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new DeactivateUserCommand(user.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["DeactivateSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["DeactivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadUsersAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                // The handler rejects self-deactivation with a friendly
                // message; surface it verbatim.
                await Toast.Error(
                    result.Error ?? Loc["ActionError"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["ActionError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    private async Task HandleActivateAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        // No confirmation for activation — it's a non-destructive restore.
        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ActivateUserCommand(user.Id));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ActivateSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["ActivateSuccessTitle"]);
                await LoadUsersAsync();
            }
            else
            {
                await Toast.Error(
                    result.Error ?? Loc["ActionError"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["ActionError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Reset password (Admin only) ─────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Prompts the admin (via the browser's native prompt()) for a new
    /// password, then dispatches ResetUserPasswordCommand. Same UX pattern
    /// as AdminProducts.razor's restock flow — simple, no custom dialog.
    ///
    /// The handler defers password-complexity validation to ASP.NET
    /// Identity's configured rules. Client-side, we just check non-empty
    /// and at least 8 chars to catch obvious typos before the round-trip.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task HandleResetPasswordAsync(UserListItemDto user)
    {
        if (_isBusyUserId.HasValue) return;

        var promptMessage = string.Format(
            CultureInfo.CurrentCulture,
            Loc["ResetPrompt"],
            user.FullName,
            user.WorkerId);

        var newPassword = await JS.InvokeAsync<string?>("prompt", promptMessage, "");

        // User clicked Cancel or pressed Escape.
        if (string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(newPassword)) return;

        newPassword = newPassword.Trim();

        // Minimal client-side check — Identity's complexity rules are
        // the real authority and will reject anything too weak.
        if (newPassword.Length < 8)
        {
            await Toast.Warning(Loc["ResetInvalidPassword"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            return;
        }

        _isBusyUserId = user.Id;
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result>(
                new ResetUserPasswordCommand(user.Id, newPassword));

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                await Toast.Success(
                    string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["ResetSuccess"], user.FullName),
                    summary: Loc["ResetSuccessTitle"]);
            }
            else
            {
                // Identity's error descriptions are user-friendly (e.g.
                // "Passwords must have at least one non-alphanumeric character.")
                // — surface verbatim.
                await Toast.Error(
                    result.Error ?? Loc["ResetError"],
                    summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
            }
        }
        catch
        {
            await Toast.Error(Loc["ResetError"], summary: Loc["ErrorTitle"]);
        }
        finally
        {
            _isBusyUserId = null;
        }
    }

    // ── Row render hook ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void OnRowRender(RowRenderEventArgs<UserListItemDto> args)
    {
        // Subtle visual cue for inactive rows: slight opacity. The status
        // badge already conveys the state, but the row-level cue helps
        // scan-by-gesture users notice deactivated accounts at a glance.
        if (args.Data is { } u && !u.IsActive)
        {
            args.Attributes.Add("style", "opacity: 0.65;");
        }
    }

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private string GetGenderLabel(Domain.Users.Gender gender)
        => gender switch
        {
            Domain.Users.Gender.Male => Loc["GenderMale"],
            Domain.Users.Gender.Female => Loc["GenderFemale"],
            _ => gender.ToString()
        };
}